{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For Irish-authorised UCITS ETFs, the transparency-policy disclosure is not necessarily a requirement to publish the full portfolio daily. The policy explains how portfolio information is provided to authorised participants (APs) and market makers to support arbitrage, and must be disclosed in the prospectus and on the ETF’s website under the 2026 regulations.\n\nThe default is daily public disclosure of holdings, generally on the ETF website, as prescribed by the regulations.\n\nPeriodic public holdings disclosure is permitted only if APs and market makers receive daily portfolio information sufficient to facilitate arbitrage, and the ETF meets the applicable regulatory conditions and procedures. It is not a blanket exemption from transparency.\n\nCBI Q&A 1012 (April 2025) addresses the periodic-disclosure route and its conditions; it does not replace the 2026 regulations or make periodic disclosure universally available."}}
